{"id": "EUVD-2026-59533", "enisaUuid": "c27e7f3c-511e-38b0-a9df-9f9b08ed2f54", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvmet-tcp: fix page fragment cache leak in error path\n\nIn nvmet_tcp_alloc_queue(), when a connection is closed during the\nallocation process (e.g., nvmet_tcp_set_queue_sock() returns -ENOTCONN),\nthe error handling jumps to out_destroy_sq and then to out_ida_remove\nwithout draining the page fragment cache.\n\nAlthough nvmet_tcp_free_cmd() is called in some error paths to release\nindividual page fragments, the underlying page cache reference held by\nqueue->pf_cache is never released. The first allocation using pf_cache\nis the call to nvmet_tcp_alloc_cmd() for queue->connect, which happens\nafter ida_alloc() returns successfully. This results in a page leak each\ntime a connection fails during allocation, which could lead to memory\nexhaustion over time if connections are repeatedly opened and closed.\n\nFix this by calling page_frag_cache_drain() before freeing the queue\nstructure in the out_ida_remove label.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:59:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc11e3f0daaadb6e600a86e54b089d4662d0a464", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a43a9abc1ebf663f0aa56a729106f68dd9c77da6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba3209704b3cd46961e4e081af5c52a780785648", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fbe83a374f09561a0f0c1f4aa021501ffd681eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4dae393956093c807212918fd91a8fc70df15338"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74386", "GHSA-3685-2pvg-g2mr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04fdf50d-7dde-3ecf-983d-81fc43395adc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "872d26a391da92ed8f0c0f5cb5fef428067b7f30 <a43a9abc1ebf663f0aa56a729106f68dd9c77da6"}, {"id": "2c211f59-869e-3bd1-96d9-59300328fd41", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "872d26a391da92ed8f0c0f5cb5fef428067b7f30 <4dae393956093c807212918fd91a8fc70df15338"}, {"id": "33148a1d-c6ba-3b68-8441-30d4de5e79ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "872d26a391da92ed8f0c0f5cb5fef428067b7f30 <ba3209704b3cd46961e4e081af5c52a780785648"}, {"id": "76a315fb-59c3-342d-a94a-2f929631ed0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "7bad4309-99e0-34de-89e2-08b754883938", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "85fa4120-6810-3873-959f-07547657ffdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "872d26a391da92ed8f0c0f5cb5fef428067b7f30 <fc11e3f0daaadb6e600a86e54b089d4662d0a464"}, {"id": "ad8aabbd-d700-3df5-ac23-764ba798461f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "b89d8f9d-8b0e-3592-bf54-b00da0c5fd4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "bb42c05f-1916-3fda-b6f4-cededff54a00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c2ae1508-c118-39fb-a9b1-85e8de3f0cd4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "d2408772-8162-3358-a36a-d47d5a2a5dee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.0"}, {"id": "f8d95011-7967-329b-8261-bfedab43887a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "872d26a391da92ed8f0c0f5cb5fef428067b7f30 <5fbe83a374f09561a0f0c1f4aa021501ffd681eb"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "673e7484-86a7-3237-8e2f-ff927786fb98", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}